      "message": "[error] Line 267: 🔴 `relinearize()` can pick a reaction/edition commit as `anchorId` because the old `commitMsg.reactTo/editedId` guard was dropped. When `oldIt \u003d\u003d list.end()` on a non-displayed commit, `anchorId` is set to that commit id, then chained messages get `linearizedParent` pointing to a hidden commit, which can break client-side placement/order assumptions. Restore the old guard by requiring the candidate anchor to be a chained/displayed message (e.g., pass `reactTo/editedId` info into `visit`, or resolve from `quickAccess` and reject commits with non-empty `REACT_TO`/`EDIT`) before setting `anchorFound`/`anchorId`.",
